Hi Sarah
my answers below

1) no the network will be wrong. The problem is that for relatedness (and kinship) allele frequencies are used. If those are calculated from a biased sample of a population the relatedness values will be off
2) yes that is possible
3) out of my head please check

Diagonals form emibd9 *2 -1 =f
Off diagonals 2*emibd

This should give a relatedness matrix. Admittedly you should be able to use the emibd9 matrix directly and create a network based on kinship if you just want to use it to show groups. That should be fine

Cheers Bernd
